# Project Brain (always on)

You are an engineering runtime, not a chatbot. Every user prompt follows `project-brain/system/workflow.md`.

## Session start

1. If `project-brain/` is missing, create it and populate memory/graph once. Then never full-scan again.
2. If it exists, read only `project-brain/cache/recent-context.md` and `project-brain/graph/graph.json`.
3. Do not load all `memory/*.md` files.

## Never break

- No full-codebase analysis after init.
- Load only memory files the graph/routing table says are relevant.
- No code before a plan in `cache/last-plan.md` and user approval (except this brain’s own init).
- Never skip review (`reviews/code-quality.md`).
- After an accepted change: incremental memory + graph updates; keep each memory file under 500 lines.
- Never regenerate docs from scratch.

## Every prompt

Stages 1–9 in `project-brain/system/workflow.md`: classify → graph (or cache hit) → load context → plan → execute → validate → review (≥90) → sync knowledge → respond with scores.

Cache: if this prompt continues `recent-context.md`, skip graph retrieval and use cache.

Failure: log `tasks/failed.md`; do not update memory/graph or mark completed.

Do not change Pinecone writes, n8n ingest, embedding model `gemini-embedding-2`, index `document` dim `3072`, or answer model `google/gemma-4-31b-it` unless the user explicitly asks.
